  "full_text": "So King David was a shepherd. He made songs. God says he prefers... He doesn't like music theory. He prefers, quote-unquote, sex with 12-year-olds. By that, he means the songs a 12-year-old might write. Well, anyway. It's like I've been marching. So here's my song. This is what I came up with. Meek and humble in heart, a twig snaps in the dark. Love it conquers all when population is small. That's my song. I don't think I can do it again. Meek and humble in heart, a twig snaps in the dark. Love it conquers all when population is small.",
